#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""blot — rewrite LSP publishDiagnostics locators; clear the origin uri.

A pure Unix filter. Never talks to git. stdin is a textDocument/
publishDiagnostics stream (JSON-RPC notification, params object,
NDJSON of Diagnostic / Location values, or LSP Content-Length frames).
Locators are 0-based `range.start.line` plus `uri` (often on a parent
params object, not a sibling). stdout is the same schema with addresses
rewritten from --from-dir onto --to-dir by content fingerprint.
Content-Length is dest-owned (UTF-8 byte length of the rewritten body).
`character` is dest-owned as UTF-16 code units, clamped to the dest line.

When every locator that bound against --from-dir moved off a
publishDiagnostics uri, emit `diagnostics: []` for that origin uri so a
client that already applied the old notification drops stale squiggles.
gist v0.2 fissioned dest files and left the origin document dirty.

SARIF `region.startLine` is 1-based and is not this schema: it is
passed through, never silently shifted. Cargo `file_name` +
`line_start` is inlay's job. SARIF nested `uri` + `startLine` is
scribe's job.
"""
